                        "review": "Even turning a profit wasn't enough to make me wanna keep playing - good game though! 😂\n\nThere's a lot of reading, text, icons and numbers, which isn't great for my ADHD.\n\nI prefer visual direction, but the tutorials only explain things once an issue comes up. I was especially confused trying to connect electricity and water. \n\nTo put it simply, the tutorial feels very messy. \n\nOnce I did get the hang of things, building was satisfying! I liked the drag and drop, the music, the sound effects and watching people move around. The management is neat too. People need electricity, water and services, while restaurants need enough customers without too much competition.\n\nHowever, when somebody moves out, I have to wait for maintenance and allocate the apartment space again. I feel like it should clean itself up and bring in a new tenant - it felt redundant for no reason.\n\nUnderstanding the systems made the game more enjoyable. I started again with offices and a layout that made more sense, and eventually turned a profit, which felt great.\n\nThere's no real stress, and you can even play with unlimited money to get the hang of things.\n\nI see the appeal, and I think it's a good game for somebody who enjoys management, building and strategy. But ultimately, it's just not something I want to keep playing.",
